1
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoes flew off too

3
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:32,980
onto the head of the carpenter I was choking

4
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:39,120
They laughed at me for still being a brat

5
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I left my energy somewhere

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:47,460
Katsushika Kameari,
even the yawns are an emergency

7
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:53,160
The unused streets are strangely gentle

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed roof of the temizuya

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,460
The sunset falls into the vast sky

10
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:15,940
Tomorrow too, this is how it ends, huh

11
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:19,740
In Katsushika Shibamata, we're happy too

12
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,420
After going all out, I realized

13
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:24,680
Because I'm such a fool

14
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:31,480
Fight on! Ryo-san

15
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:35,000
Ryotsu!

16
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,660
What's this all of a sudden, Chief?

17
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,600
What is this?!

18
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:46,600
Isn't this the incident report you
submitted all together yesterday?

19
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,340
There's not a shred of remorse in it.

20
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:52,560
Because of you,
I got a reprimand from the station chief!

21
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,320
Is that so?
I thought it was totally awesome, though.

22
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:59,480
What's awesome about
this ridiculous wording?

23
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:01,860
Your handwriting's as atrocious as ever.

24
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:04,720
At least write your own name in kanji.

25
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:07,440
Shut up, mind your own business.

26
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:12,180
On [month] [day], Heisei 10,

27
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:16,540
I took unauthorized leave from my duties in Kameari,
Katsushika Ward,

28
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:21,860
secretly used a patrol car,
and broke about three traffic laws,

29
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:23,540
and I ended up blowing it up.

30
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:28,560
My colleague Nakagawa wanted to go to the sea,
so I tried to stop him,

31
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,740
But I never said that!

32
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:35,200
From now on, I'll devote myself to my work and never do anything like this again,
so forgive me.

33
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,260
No, "forgive me" is more like
"flip the table," come on!

34
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,260
Hey, it's pretty cool, right?

35
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:42,040
I don't think you're sorry at all.

36
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:44,400
It gets even worse from the second page.

37
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:47,800
Well, "same as above."

38
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:50,140
This one too, this one too.

39
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:53,420
Who writes
"same as above" on an incident report?

40
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:57,080
The chief has gone past anger
and is completely dumbfounded.

41
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,940
It's no wonder, really.

42
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:02,760
Such a narrow-minded chief,
unable to appreciate a bit of humor.

43
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:04,720
Alright, it's done!

44
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:08,060
What do you think? It's the fleet
model that's all the rage now!

45
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:09,860
Wooden

46
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,920
You idiot!

47
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,680
Is this really the time to
be making something like this?

48
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:18,120
I rewrote the whole incident report.

49
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,860
Damn you, Chief.

50
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:26,140
Rewriting that incident report

51
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,700
ended up taking me a whole day.

52
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:29,780
That was

53
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:32,280
a hundred thousand yen

54
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:35,540
If only I hadn't bought
this antiques listing.

55
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,140
I could have bought a wooden rocking horse.

56
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,520
Well, then.

57
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,200
Ryotsu!

58
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,760
What are you doing?

59
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,480
Did you actually rewrite it properly?

60
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:48,220
Come on, I finished it properly!

61
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:51,220
Chief, what business do
you have with toys anyway?

62
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:55,620
Something like this costs 100,000 yen?

63
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:57,360
What a rip-off business.

64
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:59,680
You think so too, right?

65
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:01,100
Actually,

66
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:04,140
the day after tomorrow is my
grandson Daisuke's birthday,

67
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:06,920
Is that so?

68
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,560
It is.

69
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,420
so for his present,

70
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:12,060
he requested a rocking horse,

71
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:14,180
but I never expected it to cost 100,000 yen.

72
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:16,240
Good to hear that.

73
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:18,460
This is my chance to get back
at you for the incident report.

74
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:20,740
About how much is your budget, Chief?

75
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,100
If it's around 30,000 yen, I can manage.

76
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:25,040
Understood.

77
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,500
I'll take care of it for that 30,000 yen.

78
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,220
What?

79
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,200
Exactly the same as this one.

80
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:32,960
No, I'll make an even more
magnificent rocking horse.

81
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,620
After all,

82
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:36,960
I am a master toymaker, you know.

83
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,540
You...

84
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,680
No, when I ask you for something,

85
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,480
nothing good ever comes of it.

86
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,940
Fine, I'll give up and pick a different toy.

87
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:44,880
Chief.

88
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:49,140
Chief, don't you care what
happens to Daisuke's future?

89
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:51,280
W-what do you mean?

90
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:52,540
You see, human beings

91
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:57,720
between ages one and three, the quality of
early education greatly shapes their future.

92
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:00,160
Listen, Chief.

93
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:03,220
Early education should be
gentle on the five senses.

94
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:06,920
For hearing, for example,
classical music is said to be best, right?

95
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,400
Well, that's true.

96
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:10,360
The same goes for toys.

97
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:15,880
Building blocks are fine, but a child
won't grow up well with only those!

98
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:18,560
I see.

99
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:22,471
Toys should be made of wood,
and nothing else.

100
00:05:22,521 --> 00:05:26,400
That gentle feel of wood
affects the heart, too.

101
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:28,560
For once, you've said something worthwhile.

102
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:32,360
Daisuke's future rests
on this rocking horse!

103
00:05:33,380 --> 00:05:37,320
Fine, Ryotsu.
I'll go with thirty thousand yen.

104
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:39,220
W-what?

105
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:42,800
You can't call someone by their name
without a title when asking a favor.

106
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,240
You should at least add
"san," like anyone normally would.

107
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,180
Fine.

108
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,660
Thirty thousand yen, then, Ryotsu-san.

109
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:50,460
Can't hear you.

110
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:56,260
Poor Daisuke, stuck with a
grandpa who has no common sense.

111
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,940
I was wrong.

112
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:00,440
Please.

113
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,160
I'm begging you, Ryotsu-san.

114
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:05,080
That's how you should
have asked from the start.

115
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:07,200
Right, Ohara-kun?

116
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,000
Ohara-kun.

117
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:16,820
What's with that face? Maybe I'll just back out...
No, no, I was wrong. Please, Ryo-san.

118
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:21,000
Very well, then. I'll go buy the materials.

119
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:26,640
Did I make the wrong choice?

120
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,500
Yo! Is the production coming along?

121
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:49,260
Sorry about earlier, Mr. Ryotsu.
How's it going?

122
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:51,500
Pretty good.

123
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:54,620
I-is that so? Keep up the good work.

124
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:57,067
Chief, even if it's for Daisuke,

125
00:06:57,117 --> 00:07:01,020
isn't it bad to build it right out
in the open inside the police box?

126
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:03,160
W-well, that's true.

127
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:06,662
Ryotsu, no, Mr. Ryotsu.
Considering how it looks to the public,

128
00:07:06,712 --> 00:07:09,000
would you mind building
it in the break room?

129
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:10,705
I see.

130
00:07:10,755 --> 00:07:15,320
Then move everything here
to the break room, Ohara.

131
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,080
What did you say?

132
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:19,340
I just remembered I have something to do.
Guess I'll head home.

133
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:24,840
Fine, I'll carry it myself,
so please don't go home, Mr. Ryotsu.

134
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,740
Call me sensei.

135
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:30,320
Please don't go home, Sensei Ryotsu.

136
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,880
Well, I suppose it can't be helped.

137
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:35,040
Then hurry up and carry it, Ohara.

138
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:40,300
Speaking of which,
it's about time for lunch.

139
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:42,440
Ohara-kun, I'd like to eat eel.

140
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:45,400
If you won't let me eat it,
I think I'll just go home.

141
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,580
Nakagawa, order some eel.

142
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:48,300
Yes.

143
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:50,560
Izu's unaju, then.

144
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:53,200
That's too far! Doesn't it all
taste the same wherever you eat it?

145
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,620
Fine, whatever. Goodbye.

146
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:57,220
Wait a minute.

147
00:07:57,220 --> 00:07:58,860
Fine, I'll order it.

148
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:02,380
That was delicious.

149
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:05,860
It was worth having you go out
of your way to pick it up by car.

150
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:09,680
If it doesn't turn out well when it's finished,
you won't get off easy.

151
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:14,120
That looks pretty elaborate.

152
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:18,240
It's for kids,
so sharp corners would be dangerous.

153
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:22,760
For all your complaining,
you never cut corners on your work, do you?

154
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:24,600
Sensei, your tea is ready.

155
00:08:25,620 --> 00:08:27,440
Here you go, drink it before it gets cold.

156
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:29,380
Mm, good work.

157
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:34,160
My shoulders are so stiff.
I wonder if someone could massage them.

158
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,140
Hot!

159
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,140
Jiro!

160
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:40,900
No, I'm just kidding, U4!

161
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:45,380
I think I'm getting a
fever from being so tired.

162
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:46,880
Well, little old me is going home.

163
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:51,580
Sensei, sensei,
please let me massage your shoulders.

164
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:54,160
Now the roles are completely reversed.

165
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:57,800
This time, the senior officer
clearly has the advantage.

166
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:03,780
Is it finished?

167
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:05,920
Wow, that's really something.

168
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:08,680
It looks much more luxurious
than the one at Kiba's toy shop.

169
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:10,440
As expected of Ryo-chan.

170
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,500
Daisuke will be so happy, won't he?

171
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:15,540
Chief, I've also added some bonus features.

172
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:18,920
Please try sitting on it.

173
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:22,460
Like this?

174
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:26,520
I can hear the sound of hooves.

175
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:28,160
Please pull the reins.

176
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:33,940
So it makes the sound of a real horse neighing?
Wonderful.

177
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,480
It'll also serve as
early childhood education.

178
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:39,360
At this quality, it should sell
for even 100,000 yen, shouldn't it?

179
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,720
It still has even more amazing features!

180
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:44,660
Chief, try tipping the horse's ears down.

181
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:51,880
Which horse is going to
break away from the pack?

182
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:53,420
Okamoto-suke and Musashi-no-suke
are making their move.

183
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:54,020
Wait, what is this?

184
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:56,260
A live horse race broadcast.

185
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:57,780
Bakabōn!

186
00:09:57,780 --> 00:10:00,440
What if Daisuke grows up
to be a gambler like you?

187
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,280
Take this off.

188
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,120
I see.

189
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,020
I thought it was a good idea, though.

190
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:06,840
Understood.

191
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:09,580
Everything's set perfectly.

192
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:12,440
That's great, Chief.

193
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:15,740
I can just picture Daisuke's happy face.

194
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:16,420
Chief.

195
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:18,700
Please take care of this payment.

196
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,000
W-what is this?

197
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:24,480
I ordered sushi delivery from the
sushi shop for dinner last night.

198
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,420
What?!

199
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:28,460
If you won't pay, I can't hand this over.

200
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:32,260
If I take the toy in, I should be
able to get over 50,000 yen for it.

201
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,540
F-fine.

202
00:10:34,540 --> 00:10:36,480
Fine, I'll pay. I'll pay!

203
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,500
Thanks for your business!

204
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:41,540
Well, I'm off duty today,
so I'll be taking my leave.

205
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,480
Damn you, Ryotsu!

206
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:48,740
I'll get my revenge for this, you hear me?

207
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:58,840
Morning.

208
00:10:58,840 --> 00:10:59,660
Morning.

209
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:00,180
Morning.

210
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:01,200
Good morning.

211
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,780
That's a magnificent orchid, though.

212
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:05,660
Isn't it?

213
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:08,840
I divided the orchid I bought the other day

214
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:11,120
and raised it with great care.

215
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,400
What are you doing?

216
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:15,500
The Chief brought in the orchid
he's been growing at home.

217
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:16,440
Orchid?

218
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:19,060
It's a rather puny flower, isn't it?

219
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:21,400
It looks like a row of
dumplings from around the corner.

220
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,280
You don't need to look at it, do you?

221
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:26,080
Yeah, yeah, no need to look.

222
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:30,020
Senpai, this Phalaenopsis
orchid is a high-class flower.

223
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:32,580
How expensive is it? How much does it cost?

224
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:35,380
If you're buying one,
it's at least 30,000 yen.

225
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:39,440
What? 30,000 yen? For that dumpling-looking flower,
30,000 yen?

226
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:42,840
I can't believe it.
30,000 yen for just one little stalk?

227
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:47,420
So that means it's the same price as
the rocking horse I spent two days making?

228
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:52,160
The work I poured my heart into for
two days is worth the same as this?

229
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:53,000
How infuriating.

230
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:55,140
There's no need to cry about it.

231
00:11:55,140 --> 00:11:56,200
You saw it too, didn't you?

232
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,880
The rocking horse I made.

233
00:11:57,880 --> 00:11:59,440
That was pure master craftsmanship.

234
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,160
It was art, wasn't it?

235
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,740
Yes, it really was a splendid piece of work.

236
00:12:03,740 --> 00:12:04,220
Right?

237
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:10,060
Hey, comparing it to some weed or flower
that sprouted randomly from a garden!

238
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:11,880
The world's gone wrong.

239
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:14,020
My work is far more magnificent.

240
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:17,480
But this orchid is a magnificent work too.

241
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,140
What did you say?

242
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:22,720
Now, now, senpai.
Gardening is all the rage these days.

243
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:25,540
What's this,
some relative of the dry cleaner's?

244
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:28,560
It means growing plants and flowers at home.

245
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:32,580
Worthless flowers! All you need are
chrysanthemums for the equinox memorial services.

246
00:12:32,580 --> 00:12:34,380
We don't need such expensive flowers.

247
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:37,800
If it's the same price anyway,
I'd much rather have gotten a melon.

248
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:39,480
You're so noisy about every little thing.

249
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:40,660
Keep saying that, whatever.

250
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:44,540
You don't even try to listen
to other people's opinions.

251
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:46,900
It's the end of the world
if something like that sells.

252
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:51,980
Wait a minute.

253
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,760
So if one pot is 30,000 yen,

254
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:56,680
ten pots would be 300,000 yen.

255
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,460
A hundred pots would be 3 million yen.

256
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:01,860
If the Chief can grow them at his house,

257
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:03,320
then I can grow them too.

258
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:06,780
Hey, this might be a sweet deal after all.

259
00:13:19,140 --> 00:13:19,998
You see, orchids,

260
00:13:20,048 --> 00:13:23,320
depending on how you raise them,
they bloom again and again.

261
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:26,420
If you care for them as carefully as you do,
Chief, they'll probably bloom.

262
00:13:27,020 --> 00:13:27,720
Well, yes.

263
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:30,600
Chief.

264
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:31,700
What is it?

265
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:35,500
About how many of these
flowers do you have at home?

266
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,600
Around twenty pots, I think.

267
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:39,280
W-what, twenty pots?

268
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:41,460
So that's 600,000 yen.

269
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:43,000
It's truly a flower of money.

270
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:46,920
Chief, where do they sell
the seeds for this flower?

271
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:47,960
What? Seeds?

272
00:13:48,220 --> 00:13:50,920
You said earlier it was worthless.
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

273
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:52,240
Well, that...

274
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:55,000
Looking closer, it's a wonderful flower.

275
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:56,760
Beautiful.

276
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:59,440
What a creepy fellow you are.

277
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:02,540
No, I'm belatedly moved,

278
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:04,100
it's like scales have fallen from my eyes.

279
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:06,980
Honestly,
cardigans are truly a wonderful hobby.

280
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,100
Isn't it pretty much the same thing?

281
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,140
How so?

282
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:13,760
Hey, Chief, forget about him.

283
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:18,060
I'd like to experience the joy of growing flowers
just like you, Chief,

284
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:19,540
so please, do teach me.

285
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:22,240
Then, about a garden shop I know,

286
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,520
I'll make a note of it.

287
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,000
Something's off.

288
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,500
I have a feeling he's
up to something sinister.

289
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:32,420
Takuya, how are you feeling today?

290
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:36,240
Masahiro, Gorou, Tsuyoshi, Shingo,

291
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:39,280
Reiko-chan, Yuka-chan,
is everyone doing well?

292
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:41,180
Daddy's come to feed you.

293
00:14:41,230 --> 00:14:43,760
Eat lots and grow up to be fine adults.

294
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:47,060
Tomoya, that's good. You've grown so tall.

295
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:48,864
Ami-chan, Yumi-chan,

296
00:14:48,914 --> 00:14:51,980
don't copy the neighbor's Tamio-chan,
stand up straight, okay?

297
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:55,044
Reiko named the flowers,

298
00:14:55,094 --> 00:14:59,080
and when I advised her that talking to
them every day makes them grow faster,

299
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,900
she named all 100 of them,
and that's how it ended up.

300
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:05,960
Buying that many at once
doesn't seem like a hobby to me.

301
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,740
Ever since you found out about them

302
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:11,020
You're totally planning to
make a business out of it.

303
00:15:11,020 --> 00:15:11,820
Chief.

304
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:15,020
What temperature should the
greenhouse be kept at again?

305
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:17,460
Right now, about 15 degrees.

306
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:19,120
15 degrees, got it.

307
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:21,940
Should I put up sunshade covers?

308
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,480
You might want to start soon.

309
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:27,580
Just in case, for pest control,

310
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:29,640
I bought some Sumithion and Kelthane.

311
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:31,300
Do I need anything else?

312
00:15:32,180 --> 00:15:34,200
That should be fine for now.

313
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,180
Thanks.

314
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:38,780
He's a diligent guy, does his research.

315
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:42,020
Senpai changes completely
when money's involved.

316
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:42,880
Chief.

317
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:45,520
Don't just show up out of nowhere.

318
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:48,840
Sorry, about dividing the plants...

319
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:51,280
Suddenly acting all humble

320
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:55,440
Right, this is payback for
the rocking horse the other day.

321
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:59,300
Chief, didn't you hear me?
It's dividing the plants.

322
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:01,000
Dividing what?

323
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,880
That's an important point, you know.

324
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:05,540
Right? So how do you do it well?

325
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:08,260
Darn, my shoulders have gotten stiff.

326
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:11,860
What? Damn it, are you trying
to get revenge for the other day?

327
00:16:12,260 --> 00:16:14,400
I wish someone would knead my shoulders.

328
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:16,380
That's better. Much better.

329
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:20,780
Sorry, Ryotsu,
having you massage my shoulders like this.

330
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:23,480
It's nothing at all.

331
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:25,360
So how do you divide them?

332
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:29,560
Dividing them wrong can damage the roots.
It's difficult.

333
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:32,580
That's why I'm asking
you to teach me the method.

334
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:33,600
I'm back.

335
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,240
Ryo-chan,
you're off duty and you still came in?

336
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:38,620
I have to look after the gardening shop,
after all.

337
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:41,220
Chief, I bought some new tea.

338
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:43,640
Let's all drink it right away.

339
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,680
Ryotsu says he'll make it for everyone.

340
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,320
I'm off duty, you know.

341
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,820
Why should I have to make it?

342
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:52,040
Don't you want my advice, then?

343
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:54,300
Fine, I'll just do it myself.

344
00:16:54,980 --> 00:16:55,540
I see.

345
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,040
Well, good luck, then.

346
00:16:57,040 --> 00:17:00,400
Orchids are weak against disease,
so be very careful.

347
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:03,260
There have been cases where
they were wiped out overnight.

348
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,260
Don't be so heartless and mean.
Please teach me.

349
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:13,380
Damn it,
taking advantage of my weakness like that!

350
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:14,940
It's about time for lunch, isn't it?

351
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:17,160
Shall we all have some sushi?

352
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:22,540
Sounds great!
We just got paid, so let's splurge for once.

353
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,020
No, no, you don't have to pay out of your own pocket.
Ryotsu says he'll treat us.

354
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:27,340
I knew it!

355
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:30,040
How cruel! No way!

356
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:32,500
If you don't like it,
then teach me how to divide the orchids!

357
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:36,080
Damn it, we're at a huge disadvantage here.

358
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:38,880
Four orders of the premium nigiri, please.

359
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:43,380
Right, could we go to Matsu Sushi in Ueno?

360
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:45,180
All the way over there!

361
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:46,200
Yes.

362
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:57,980
Everyone, listen to good
music and grow up refined, okay?

363
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:06,740
Excuse me. Could you throw back our ball?

364
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:08,340
You lot!

365
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:12,080
Don't play baseball in the park!

366
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:16,120
You broke Shinji-chan and Naomi-chan's pot!

367
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:17,600
Don't give me that!

368
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:18,580
Shut up!

369
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,340
Honestly.

370
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:30,340
Hey, wait!

371
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:33,340
Whoa! Crows again!

372
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:35,640
Don't you dare eat Yukio and Naoto!

373
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,280
Get away!

374
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:38,780
Come on!

375
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:45,000
If it comes to this,
we'll guard them round the clock!

376
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:55,600
Senpai, why don't you take a
nap at the police box at night?

377
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:57,640
No way! Gardening is a battle!

378
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:00,680
Weather check!

379
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:01,780
Ichiro, check!

380
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:03,180
Hideki, check!

381
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:04,500
Nomo, check!

382
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:05,400
Pai-chan, check!

383
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:06,120
Ai-chan, check!

384
00:19:06,340 --> 00:19:06,900
Tomoko, check!

385
00:19:07,340 --> 00:19:07,860
Yukiyo!

386
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:10,680
So Yukiyo got eaten
without us even noticing.

387
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,324
Your enthusiasm is admirable, but

388
00:19:17,374 --> 00:19:20,260
I wonder if Ryo-chan will
last until the flowers bloom?

389
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,720
I'm risking my life here, senpai.

390
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,060
What the hell?!

391
00:19:28,980 --> 00:19:30,220
Aaaaaah!

392
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:37,680
Sorry, we got lost! Don't go
driving through regular city streets!

393
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:39,400
Aaaaaah!

394
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,820
It's an earthquake! Laurel, watch out!

395
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:48,340
Top Gun-kun, Michael-kun, Jozan-kun

396
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:49,200
Nooooo!

397
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,560
Why is there a tornado?

398
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:57,820
Otomo Gabriel

399
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:02,140
Please don't take my precious children!

400
00:20:06,620 --> 00:20:07,340
Shoo, shoo!

401
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:08,740
It bloomed!

402
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:17,480
I never expected you'd
get fifty pots to bloom!

403
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,460
Beautiful.

404
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:21,520
Chief, all your hard work has paid off.

405
00:20:24,180 --> 00:20:29,080
Right, let's have an appraiser
figure out how much these are worth.

406
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:34,520
Wow, it's been ages since I've
seen such magnificent orchids.

407
00:20:35,060 --> 00:20:36,960
So, how much is one pot worth?

408
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,720
At this quality,
it should be at least 50,000 yen.

409
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:41,300
50,000 yen.

410
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:42,460
That much?

411
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:45,520
So fifty of them come to 2.5 million yen

412
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:47,940
Well, I'm impressed.

413
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:50,580
What's wrong?

414
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,280
Take a look at this.

415
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:55,260
It's turned purple.

416
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:56,400
What's so special about this?

417
00:20:57,680 --> 00:20:59,680
They sometimes turn pink or red,

418
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,300
but turning purple is rare.

419
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:03,760
At this rate, it's worth 500,000,
no, a million yen.

420
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:06,600
You're Kuma-san!

421
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:08,240
What a devoted child you are!

422
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:11,100
There might be more of them, you know.

423
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:12,440
Let me take a look.

424
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:14,060
Found one!

425
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:15,600
Hatsu-san has turned purple too!

426
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:18,680
Kuma-san and Hatsu-san
alone are worth 2 million yen

427
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:19,740
Yes, yes, that's the spirit!

428
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:22,560
Is blue not good?

429
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:24,340
Even blue?

430
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:28,300
It's a miracle,
a blue this beautiful appearing!

431
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:33,000
Even with roses, they say getting blue
flowers to bloom is extremely difficult.

432
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:37,140
For this, there are people who'd pay five million,
no, ten million yen.

433
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:40,780
Ten million yen.

434
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:43,860
Jigen Buji Game No. 5, Surikire-kun.

435
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:46,180
Just as expected,
it was worth giving it such a long name.

436
00:21:47,060 --> 00:21:48,660
Papa's so happy!

437
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:52,688
Ryo-san, tomorrow there's an orchid
exhibition at the ward botanical garden.

438
00:21:52,738 --> 00:21:54,720
You should take them all there.

439
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:58,060
If they win a prize,
they might fetch an even higher price.

440
00:21:58,680 --> 00:21:59,460
Alright, got it.

441
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:07,502
Fifty pots is pretty heavy, even for us.

442
00:22:07,552 --> 00:22:09,120
Shall we take a little break?

443
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,460
Just having them appraised,
they're worth 15 million yen.

444
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:17,100
If we add a box for the exhibition,
it's 30 million.

445
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:19,840
Or maybe it'll even go
up to around 50 million!

446
00:22:21,820 --> 00:22:24,920
This is all thanks to
you two working so hard.

447
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,880
Still, I do have a real
talent for gardening.

448
00:22:28,380 --> 00:22:30,940
Maybe I should quit the police
and make this my main job.

449
00:22:34,120 --> 00:22:34,840
Oh no!

450
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:36,600
Nobody move!

451
00:22:37,420 --> 00:22:39,580
Next game, next game...
Is that a worn-out No. 5 ball?

452
00:22:41,740 --> 00:22:42,700
Nice game!

453
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:45,140
I'm saving you all right now!

454
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:49,320
Get in front and stop that handcart!

455
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:53,180
I'll protect them even
if it costs me my life!

456
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:57,780
We did it!

457
00:22:58,740 --> 00:23:00,200
Uh-oh, this is bad!

458
00:23:04,580 --> 00:23:06,900
So this orchid is worth 20 million yen?

459
00:23:07,540 --> 00:23:12,220
Apparently it's been passed down from
the orchid Marie Antoinette adored.

460
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:14,000
Aaaaaah!

461
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,620
Aaaaaah!

462
00:23:15,620 --> 00:23:16,980
Aaaaaah!

463
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:19,600
Eeeeeeh!

464
00:23:22,180 --> 00:23:23,500
Eeeeeeh!

465
00:23:23,500 --> 00:23:26,040
Aaaaaah!

466
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:26,900
Aaaaaah!

467
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:27,940
Aaaaaah!

468
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:29,800
Aaaaaah!

469
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:30,160
Aaaaaah!

470
00:23:32,660 --> 00:23:34,100
What have you done?!

471
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:38,440
Those orchids that were displayed here are worth fifty million yen in total,
you know.

472
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:40,240
W-what?!

473
00:23:41,460 --> 00:23:42,880
Chief, boss!

474
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:44,340
I-I don't know anything about it!

475
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:45,540
Ohara, don't get involved.

476
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:46,340
Let's go.

477
00:23:46,340 --> 00:23:46,580
Yes.

478
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:49,340
Please wait.

479
00:23:49,740 --> 00:23:51,320
You're going to make us pay for it,
you know.

480
00:23:51,320 --> 00:23:53,700
I-it was just an accident like that...

481
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:54,760
Chief.

482
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:56,940
I don't know anything about it, you hear?

483
00:23:56,940 --> 00:23:58,860
Sort it out yourself.

484
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:09,700
That Volvo guy has finally been
assigned to the Katsushika police box.

485
00:24:09,700 --> 00:24:11,640
And then Jodie showed up too,

486
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:14,200
saying he wants a rematch with Volvo.

487
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:17,560
Volvo, you'd better do something
about that nosebleed first.

488
00:24:18,140 --> 00:24:21,320
Next time, catch Volvo's Living Together Days.
See you then!

489
00:24:35,800 --> 00:24:55,700
Surprise and commotion, spirit and resolution, quick action, lending a hand, decided,
a flash of inspiration, bouncing along, gathered together, taking action, flying away.

490
00:24:56,740 --> 00:25:00,460
The most incredible power of all.

491
00:25:00,460 --> 00:25:06,420
Everyone gather here,

492
00:25:07,340 --> 00:25:12,660
the dreamlike, ultimate energy.

493
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,140
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday,

494
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:20,040
painting the universe,
and standing on the earth,

495
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:23,840
the Kameari star spun around in a circle.

496
00:25:26,220 --> 00:25:27,380
That's good enough, right?

497
00:25:27,380 --> 00:25:29,040
Like hell it is!

